353 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 169 0 R/E(Use these activities to get a feel for how visualisation can feel! Please don\220t worry if you don\220t nail it the first time! Practise makes perfect! You can spend time visualising you positive birth as often as you like, it\220s a fab way to change your mindset and send oxytocin to your baby!)/Pg 20 0 R/K[0]>>
endobj

354 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 169 0 R/E(1. First you can have a partner or friend listen to you for 5 mins \(or record\) telling your birth story as if it\220s already happened. Tell it in as much detail as possible, how did you feel? Who was there? Where were you? What happened when? Make it as positive as you like, this is supposed to be YOUR perfect birth. If you would like to complete this activity alone, just set a timer and get chatting. Go with the flow and see what amazing birth story you can come up with and imagine it\220s yours! How do you feel now? A bit silly? That\220s alright! Do you feel motivated to go and get that birth you were just visualising? Go and get it!)/Pg 20 0 R/K[1]>>
endobj

355 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 169 0 R/E(2. Write your birth story in the past tense, this can be done as well as the previous activity to see which one you prefer! Some people don\220t find it easy to visualise. Read through your finished story and see how you feel! Does it make you feel like your birth could be as positive as that? Are you feeling really pumped about it? It\220s working!)/Pg 20 0 R/K[2]>>
endobj

356 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 169 0 R/E(3, Create a vision board to help you based on the key points from your story \(e.,g,. fairy lights, birth pool, your partner etc.)/Pg 20 0 R/K[3]>>
endobj

