376 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 171 0 R/E(Pelvic Floor Exercises)/Pg 22 0 R/K[0]>>
endobj

377 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 171 0 R/E(- You do these twice a day, every day. No excuses. This is something that can make sure your life and your sex life stay happy and healthy and absolutely no wetting your pants! It\220s just as important to focus on the release too- we need a floppy pelvic floor for birth! Do quick ones \(think \217on-off\220\) longer ones holding for 3 seconds then releasing and then longer ones for 10 seconds or more. Repeat a few times.)/Pg 22 0 R/K[1]>>
endobj

378 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 171 0 R/E(Perineal massage)/Pg 22 0 R/K[2]>>
endobj

379 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 171 0 R/E(- Practice this daily from 36 weeks but only if you fancy it. Some people swear by it to reduce tearing and others don\220t enjoy it one bit and would rather not. You do you!)/Pg 22 0 R/K[3]>>
endobj

380 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 171 0 R/E(Massage)/Pg 22 0 R/K[4]>>
endobj

381 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 171 0 R/E(- Encourage your birth partner to practice various massage techniques regularly so that they are a pro by the time you\220re in labour, these can be used to increase your oxytocin both in pregnancy and in labour and help you feel more comfortable.)/Pg 22 0 R/K[5]>>
endobj

382 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 171 0 R/E(Prenatal bonding)/Pg 22 0 R/K[6]>>
