982 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H2/P 216 0 R/T(What happened during active labour?)/E(What happened during active labour?)/Pg 67 0 R/K[4]>>
endobj

983 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 216 0 R/E(Did your waters break in the middle of the supermarket? Did you think you had the shits because of the sensations? Were you induced?)/Pg 67 0 R/K[5]>>
endobj

984 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 216 0 R/E(What did you do to keep comfortable? Did you do any activities? Did you go out an- ywhere? Did you have anything yummy to eat? Who was with you? Did you watch or listen to anything?)/Pg 67 0 R/K[6]>>
endobj

985 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 216 0 R/E(Did you feel a change in intensity? Were interventions offered? Did you feel like everything was explained to you and your decisions respected? Did you or your birth partner recognise the transition phase of labour? Did you feel the urge to push? What position were you in as baby was born? Was your baby born in a theatre with forceps or caesarean? How did that change to your birth plan feel?)/Pg 67 0 R/K[7]>>
endobj

986 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 216 0 R/E(Did you have any particular pregnancy symptoms? Any special circumstances for your- self or baby? How did you feel about labour and birth? What antenatal education or reading did you do to prepare? What type of birth were you planning? How did you feel in the days before baby was born? Were there any signs labour was coming? )/Pg 67 0 R/K[8]>>
endobj

987 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 216 0 R/E(Writing your birth story can be a really lovely thing to do after a positive birth, it can also be really healing when birth didn\220t go as you hoped. You can do it anytime at all after your baby is born. If you\220d like to do it when your baby is newborn or 20 years old, crack on!)/Pg 67 0 R/K[9]>>
endobj

988 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 216 0 R/E(Here are some prompts to help you include everything\203.)/Pg 67 0 R/K[10]>>
endobj

989 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 216 0 R/E(How did you recognise it was time to head to your birth space or call for a midwife to attend? How was the journey? How did you feel? Did setting up your birth space go well? What did you use to keep comfortable? How was your progress assessed? Did you have any vaginal exams or observations? Did you use a birth pool or have any pain relief? What did your birth partner/s do that was helpful? How were the staff?)/Pg 67 0 R/K[11]>>
endobj

990 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H1/P 216 0 R/T(writing your birth story)/E(writing your birth story)/Pg 67 0 R/K[12]>>
endobj

991 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 217 0 R/E(What were your first thoughts as you met your baby face to face for the first time? Who was the first person to touch your baby. How were baby and you immediately after birth? How did you birth the placenta? Did you change locations after baby was born? \(getting out of a pool, laying on a bed, moving rooms or to a ward etc\). Did you have any stitches? Were you already home or how long did you stay in hospital if relevant.)/Pg 68 0 R/K[0]>>
endobj

992 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 217 0 R/E(That should cover all the basics to help prompt you to remember the various parts, you may feel like you need to ask someone else who was there about the details, that\220s perfect- ly normal!)/Pg 68 0 R/K[1]>>
endobj

993 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 217 0 R/E(Your birth story can be just for you to treasure or you could share it with the world!)/Pg 68 0 R/K[2]>>
endobj

