endobj

2228 0 obj
<</Title(Download the birth planning guide to access your free templates for both vaginal and caesarean births.)/Dest[44 0 R/Fit]/Parent 7 0 R/Prev 2230 0 R/Next 2224 0 R>>
endobj

2229 0 obj
<</Title(Birthing the placenta)/Dest[41 0 R/Fit]/Parent 7 0 R/Prev 2227 0 R/Next 2231 0 R>>
endobj

2230 0 obj
<</Title(Change your birth plan any time you want, we often learn new things and make new choices. Finally, you can change your mind on the day if you want to!)/Dest[44 0 R/Fit]/Parent 7 0 R/Prev 2232 0 R/Next 2228 0 R>>
endobj

2231 0 obj
<</Title(birth planning)/Dest[42 0 R/Fit]/Parent 7 0 R/Prev 2229 0 R/Next 2233 0 R>>
endobj

2232 0 obj
<</Title(Do this with your birth partner ideally so that they understand it all and know the reasons for your choices. At the very least, go through it in detail with them, they will then be able to help relay it to your care providers on the day.)/Dest[44 0 R/Fit]/Parent 7 0 R/Prev 2234 0 R/Next 2230 0 R>>
endobj

2233 0 obj
<</Title(Talk through your options with knowledgable folks. Your instructor or the AIMS helpline would be a good start, they can tell you what they know, any relevant research and help you come up with a list of questions for you to ask your care providers as well as stuff to read up on.)/Dest[43 0 R/Fit]/Parent 7 0 R/Prev 2231 0 R/Next 2235 0 R>>
endobj

2234 0 obj
<</Title(Would you like baby wiped down before you hold them? This is all up to you! Finally, how would you like to birth the placenta? What would you like to do with it after?)/Dest[44 0 R/Fit]/Parent 7 0 R/Prev 2236 0 R/Next 2232 0 R>>
endobj

2235 0 obj
<</Title(Discuss with your care provider. This may be a midwife or a consultant, do not be disheartened if you don\220t hear what you would like to hear, you can still chat through your circumstances with a Professional Midwifery Advocate and they can talk you through if what you are after is REALLY out of the question or not.)/Dest[43 0 R/Fit]/Parent 7 0 R/Prev 2233 0 R/Next 2237 0 R>>
endobj

2236 0 obj
<</Title(What about vitamin K injection for baby? Let those reading know how you would like to feed your baby and what you would like to happen with baby when they are born, would you like uninterrupted skin to skin?)/Dest[44 0 R/Fit]/Parent 7 0 R/Prev 2238 0 R/Next 2234 0 R>>
endobj

2237 0 obj
<</Title(Consider what things are super important to you and you would not like to miss out on unless theres an emergency. This may be remaining upright throughout labour and for the birth, skin to skin after birth, avoiding \217the drip\220 or any other intervention or medication etc. How can you try to make sure that you can have these things? Can they be worked into all your birth plans? Eg. Remaining upright- even in the case of epidural use you can be assisted into various positions that support birth. Skin to skin after birth, can it be arranged that your birth partner holds baby on your chest for skin to skin EVEN after a Caesarean under general anaesthetic? Avoiding \217the drip\220, this may mean you opt for a caesarean if you would rather. There are so many possibilities we\220re not always offered, if you aren\220t sure how you can still incorporate certain things then talk to your instructor!)/Dest[43 0 R/Fit]/Parent 7 0 R/Prev 2235 0 R/Next 2239 0 R>>
endobj

2238 0 obj
<</Title(Who will cut the cord? When will it be clamped \(if at all\)?)/Dest[44 0 R/Fit]/Parent 7 0 R/Prev 2240 0 R/Next 2236 0 R>>
endobj

2239 0 obj
<</Title(Create the birth plans for real! Consider everything you\220ve learned about any factors concerning your pregnancy and chats with PMA or midwife etc and bring it all together to create your plan using whichever format suits you best, try to ensure it will be easily read by the care providers and explained by your birth partner.)/Dest[43 0 R/Fit]/Parent 7 0 R/Prev 2237 0 R/Next 2241 0 R>>
endobj

2240 0 obj
<</Title(Then consider what you would like to happen once baby is here, would you like to find out the sex yourself?)/Dest[44 0 R/Fit]/Parent 7 0 R/Prev 2242 0 R/Next 2238 0 R>>
endobj

2241 0 obj
<</Title(Create your plan methodically by first considering your background such as how you feel about birth, how many babies you\220ve had, any special medical or cultural requirements.)/Dest[43 0 R/Fit]/Parent 7 0 R/Prev 2239 0 R/Next 2243 0 R>>
endobj

2242 0 obj
<</Title(Next consider what you would like for each stage of labour, comfort measures you\220d like to have available, what monitoring or interventions you would like to choose or avoid. Make sure to include what you would like your midwives to do, whether you would prefer them in the background or if you would really like the reassurance of having them right next to you when they\220re in the room. Include how you would like baby to be born, whether you would like direction from a caregiver or not and if you would be happy to accept forceps etc if thought necessary.)/Dest[43 0 R/Fit]/Parent 7 0 R/Prev 2243 0 R/Next 2240 0 R>>
endobj

2243 0 obj
<</Title(Then move onto the things that you would like to include in your environment such as low light levels, quiet, who you would like present \(eg. Are you happy to have student midwives present? A doula?\).)/Dest[43 0 R/Fit]/Parent 7 0 R/Prev 2241 0 R/Next 2242 0 R>>
endobj

